theorem `site_avoidance` proves `∀ C, HolePlacement holes (concreteProgram C)`
for every `holes ⊆ physicalHoles` from per-piece facts:

* every piece of the literal program is listed once, together with the map
  that sends its own labels to physical wires (`U` for the finite stage,
  `UG = U ∘ swap ∘ rho` for the generic block, `kernelPlace` for kernel labels,
  `phasePlace = kernelPlace ∘ phaseHost` for the two phases, `lowPlace` for the
  un-borrowed field level, `StairPhysicalInventory.place` for the field tail);
* a piece fact is `PieceOK holes f P`: arena and old-hole freedom (`ArenaOld`)
  plus freedom of the given holes (`HolesFree`);
* the staircase pieces (all forward/reverse segments, `forwardLast`,
  `reverseLast` with the v3 terminals and the s505-fixed reverse middle, the
  parity setup and hosted X) are PROVED here for every sublist of the 44 holes;
* every other piece is a named field of `OpenPieces holes` (owners in the
  report).  `record_ok` / `rec_stage` / `rec_borrowOut` already transport the
  record's own arena and old-hole theorems to two frame pieces; the remaining
  frame extractions are pending.
